  "comments": "Three main types are known.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Obverse</span><br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">1</span> - at bottom of the coat of arms out of left stalks one starts from ribbon and other 3 start from right ones.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">2</span> - at bottom of the coat of arms out of left stalks 3 start from ribbon and one starts from right stalks.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Reverse</span><br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span> - without mint mark &quot;A&quot; at the top.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span> - mint mark &quot;A&quot; at the top.<br />\r\nPicture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/64948d7d5c723.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/64948d7d5c723.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"111\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Combinations</span><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">1</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span>: 1969, 1971.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">1</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span>: 1972-1974, 1979-1981, 1981 PS, 1982-1985, 1986-1988 MS.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">2</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span>: 1989, 1989 PS, 1990 MS.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Abbreviations</span><br />\r\nMS - mint set.<br />\r\nPS - proof set.<br /><br />\r\nCorrespondence with catalog <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Die deutschen Münzen seit 1871</span> by Kurt Jaeger and Michael Kurt Sonntag.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span> - J# 1511a.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B </span>- J# 1511b.<br /><br />\r\nFormerly AKS#706 and AKS#406.",
